- helm
- net
- pass
- grove_template
- grove_install
- scope
- weave

' The foot that runs a scope's rules (scope.foil). It is told each commit,
' reads the world as it then stands, and asks for the writes the rules
' answer. The rules settle, so when nothing is due nothing is written and
' the foot is not told again.
'
' What it tends is said by records beneath its own, /<self>/io/scope: one
' that holds a reference in the slot root is a scope this world keeps (its
' places are tended and its catalog told to its members); one that holds a
' number in the slot scope is a scope this world is listed in (the worlds
' that scope lists are met). One that holds a number in the slot maker is a
' composition this world takes part in (weave.foil): maker is the world
' that keeps it, rel where it sits there, and side a reference to where
' this world keeps what it writes of it. What the composition's table says
' this world must write into others' roots is written. One that holds a
' number in the slot to is a joining: what a door wrote when it was handed
' a link (scope/join). It becomes a record of the other kinds once the
' claim it asked for is made. One that holds a reference in the slot make
' asks for a composition to be made here from the Grove unit it names, at
' rel: the unit's template is mounted there, the unit's table is written
' beneath it, and the record becomes one that keeps a scope and takes part
' in a composition, both at once. So a template is a Grove unit and
' nothing beside it. The foot stops when its record is removed or holds
' `stop`.
+ scope_foot
  + task
    & feet/task/ack
      feet/task/fact
      feet/task/admitted
      feet/task/committed
      feet/task/state
  + home
    \ self=iota
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'scope]
  + rooted
    ' The root a record names, or none.
    \ record=myth
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['root]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    | ./some link.path
  + sided
    ' The side a record names, or none.
    \ record=myth
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['side]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    | ./some link.path
  + part
    ' The composition a record says this world takes part in, with its
    ' table as this world holds it from the maker, and this world's side
    ' of it. None when the record says none.
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ maybe[[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]]
    = none=maybe[[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]] .none
      maker record.nat_at(['maker] 0)
    ? (eq 0 maker) none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse record.txt_at(['rel])) none
    ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/sided record) none
    = s (weave/side (quip_val state.self) root)
      c (weave/comp maker rel (weave/rows maker rel s state))
    | ./some [c s]
  + woven
    ' What a composition this world takes part in asks it to write: each
    ' record of its own for that record's readers, an answer to each ask
    ' of an action on a thing it writes (weave/answers), and the proof for
    ' each place where it chose to show something (scope_foot/shown).
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) none
    = [c s] found
    | (weave/tell c s state).weld((weave/answers c s state)).weld((scope_foot/shown record state))
  + parts
    ' Every composition this world takes part in.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ row[[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]]
    = none=row[[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]] []
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) acc
      | acc.snoc(found)
  + shown
    ' The proof for each showing place this world chose to fill: what it
    ' holds, in whichever composition it takes part in, of what the place
    ' wants. Where it holds nothing of it, the place is left as it is.
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) none
    = [c s] found
      all (scope_foot/parts state)
    | (weave/owes c s state).fold none
      \ out=row[[p=path q=writ]] owed=[place=path want=weave/want]
      ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
      = [place want] owed
      = empty=row[pass/witness] []
        proof
          | all.fold empty
            \ acc=row[pass/witness] other=[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]
            ^ row[pass/witness]
            = [oc os] other
            | acc.weld((weave/show oc os want state))
      ? (eq 0 proof.len) out
      = target=path s.root.weld(place)
        slot=myth (myth/sing ['proof] (pails/n (pass/shown proof)))
        change=[p=path q=writ] [target (writ/poke slot)]
      | out.snoc(change)
  + shape
    ' The table of a composition this world takes part in, as text, a
    ' line a row: where the row sits, who writes there, who reads, the
    ' action a record there asks for, what it must show, and the slots a
    ' record there may hold (weave/fields). It is what a form or a tool is
    ' made from. None when no record of that name says one.
    \ name=iota state=namespace
    ^ maybe[str]
    = none=maybe[str] .none
      at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).snoc(name)
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil none
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) none
    = [c s] found
      empty=row[str] []
      lines
        | c.table.fold empty
          \ out=row[str] p=weave/position
          ^ row[str]
          ? (weave/describes p) out
          = readers (str/join " " p.readers.map((\ w=weave/who (weave/said w))))
            slots (str/join " " (weave/fields p state))
            line (str/cat_all ["row /" (weave/spelled p.path) " | by " (weave/said p.writer) " | for " readers " | apply " p.apply " | shows " p.shows " | slots " slots])
          | out.snoc(line)
    | ./some (str/join (str/from_atom 10) lines)
  + fill
    ' Where this world would write a record at a place of a composition it
    ' takes part in, by the name of the record beneath the foot's own that
    ' says so. The place must be this world's to write now (weave/writable)
    ' and the record must have the shape its row gives (weave/fits).
    ' Otherwise why not. Whatever shows a composition to a person or to an
    ' agent writes through this and through nothing else, so neither holds
    ' a rule of its own.
    \ name=iota where=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ either[str path]
    = at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).snoc(name)
      unknown=str "No record of that name says this world takes part in a composition."
    ?> (./some held) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil (./err unknown)
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part held state) (./err unknown)
    = [c s] found
    ? !(weave/writable c s where state) (./err "That place is not this world's to write now.")
    ?> (./some row) (weave/find c where) (./err "No row of the table puts that place.")
    ? !(weave/fits row.pos record state) (./err "The record has not the shape its row gives.")
    | ./ok s.root.weld(where)
  + packs
    ' The packs this world holds, a name a line: the Grove units it
    ' publishes that carry a template, which is what a composition is
    ' made from (made).
    \ state=namespace
    ^ str
    = none=row[str] []
      base=path [state.self 'gov]
      lines
        | (sovereign_peek base state).tap.fold none
          \ acc [rel record]
          ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
          ? !(maybe/is_some record.get(grove_templates/slot)) acc
          = shown (path_show rel)
          | acc.snoc(shown.slice(1 shown.len))
    | str/join (str/from_atom 10) lines
  + took
    ' How many places beneath one were taken under a ticket, and how many
    ' of those under this one.
    \ base=path ticket=nat state=namespace
    ^ [all=nat mine=nat]
    = all
        | (sovereign_peek base state).tap.fold 0
          \ n [rel seat]
          ? !(eq rel.len 1) n
          ? (eq 0 seat.nat_at(['ticket] 0)) n
          | n.inc
      mine
        | (sovereign_peek base state).tap.fold 0
          \ n [rel seat]
          ? !(eq rel.len 1) n
          ? !(eq ticket seat.nat_at(['ticket] 0)) n
          | n.inc
    [all mine]
  + taking
    ' An open place gives a new place beneath it to whoever shows a
    ' ticket. A place is open because whoever writes it said so there: the
    ' slot open holds how many may be taken, and that is ordinary state.
    ' The new place starts as whatever else the open place's record
    ' holds, and holds the ticket and the next invitation number this
    ' world has not used, so its name is minted, its link made and its
    ' world asked for like any other invited place. It is written only
    ' where this world could write it anyway (scope_foot/fill). A ticket
    ' takes one place: shown again, it takes nothing more. Otherwise why
    ' not.
    \ name=iota where=path ticket=nat state=namespace
    ^ either[str row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).snoc(name)
      unknown=str "No record of that name says this world takes part in a composition."
      shut=str "That place is not open."
    ? (eq 0 ticket) (./err "Show a ticket: a secret of your own making.")
    ?> (./some held) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil (./err unknown)
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part held state) (./err unknown)
    = [c s] found
      base=path s.root.weld(where)
    ?> (./some place) (sovereign_care .x base state).fil (./err shut)
    = limit place.nat_at(['open] 0)
      [all mine] (scope_foot/took base ticket state)
    ? (eq 0 limit) (./err shut)
    ? (gt mine 0) (./ok none)
    ? (ge all limit) (./err "Every place offered there is taken.")
    ?> (./some tail) (path_parse (str/cat_all ["/o" (nat/show (mod ticket 1000000000000000))])) (./err shut)
    = seat=path where.weld(tail)
      record=myth place.del(['open]).put(['invite] (pails/n (scope_foot/highest state).inc)).put(['ticket] (pails/n ticket))
    ? (scope_foot/fill name seat record state)
     > (./err why) (./err why)
     > (./ok target) (./ok [[target (writ/make record)]])
  + inviting
    ' A place that holds no invitation is given one: the next number this
    ' world has not used. Its name is then minted and its link made like
    ' any invited place's (scope/tend). Only where the place stands and is
    ' this world's to write; a place that holds a number already keeps it.
    ' Otherwise why not.
    \ name=iota where=path state=namespace
    ^ either[str row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).snoc(name)
      unknown=str "No record of that name says this world takes part in a composition."
    ?> (./some held) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil (./err unknown)
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part held state) (./err unknown)
    = [c s] found
      target=path s.root.weld(where)
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x target state).fil (./err "Nothing stands at that place yet.")
    ? (gt record.nat_at(['invite] 0) 0) (./ok none)
    ? !(weave/writable c s where state) (./err "That place is not this world's to write now.")
    | ./ok [[target (writ/poke (myth/sing ['invite] (pails/n (scope_foot/highest state).inc)))]]
  + ticket
    ' The invitation's number of the place taken under a ticket, in
    ' whichever scope this world keeps; 0 when none was.
    \ ticket=nat state=namespace
    ^ nat
    ? (eq 0 ticket) 0
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold 0
      \ found [rel record]
      ? (gt found 0) found
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) found
      ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted record) found
      | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold 0
        \ id [place seat]
        ? (gt id 0) id
        ? !(eq ticket seat.nat_at(['ticket] 0)) id
        | seat.nat_at(['invite] 0)
  + offers
    ' Every open place of the scopes this world keeps, a line each: the
    ' record that names the composition, the place, how many are left to
    ' take, and what the composition and the place are called. Tabs part
    ' them. It names no world and no member: it is what the door shows
    ' nobody.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ str
    = none=row[str] []
      tab (str/from_atom 9)
      lines
        | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
          \ acc [rel record]
          ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
          ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted record) acc
          = called (sovereign_care .x root state).fil.fall((myth/sing ['title] (pails/t ""))).txt_at(['title])
          | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold acc
            \ out [place seat]
            = limit seat.nat_at(['open] 0)
              [all mine] (scope_foot/took root.weld(place) 0 state)
            ? (eq 0 limit) out
            ? (ge all limit) out
            | out.snoc((str/join tab [(path_show rel) (path_show place) (nat/show (sub limit all)) called seat.txt_at(['title])]))
    | str/join (str/from_atom 10) lines
  + view
    ' A composition this world takes part in, as it stands for this
    ' world, by the name of the record beneath the foot's own that says
    ' so (weave/laid, as text), and after it a line for each record that
    ' must show something and does not, with why (weave/doubts). None when
    ' no such record says one.
    \ name=iota state=namespace
    ^ maybe[str]
    = none=maybe[str] .none
      at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).snoc(name)
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil none
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) none
    = [c s] found
    = said=row[str] [(weave/shown (weave/laid c s state))]
    | ./some (str/join (str/from_atom 10) said.weld((weave/doubts c s state)))
  + due
    ' What one record beneath the foot's own asks for, as the world stands.
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      member record.nat_at(['scope] 0)
      taken (? (eq 0 member) none (scope/take member state))
      asked taken.weld((scope_foot/woven record state))
    ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted record) asked
    | asked.weld((scope/tended root state)).weld((scope/told root state))
  + all
    ' Everything due, for every record beneath the foot's own.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      = at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).weld(rel)
      | acc.weld((scope_foot/due record state)).weld((scope/joined at record state)).weld((scope_foot/made at record state))
  + refused
    ' Why what a record asks for came to nothing, said on the record, once.
    \ at=path record=myth reason=iota
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      said=str (iota_show reason)
      told=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke (myth/sing ['why] (pails/t said)))]]
    ? (equal[str] said record.txt_at(['why])) none
    told
  + planted
    ' The write that mounts a unit's template at a target; or, where it
    ' cannot be mounted, why.
    \ at=path record=myth source=path target=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    ?> (./some version) state.case(.x source) (scope_foot/refused at record 'scope_unpublished)
    ? (grove_install/planted source version target state)
     > (./ok writes) writes
     > (./err reason) (scope_foot/refused at record reason)
  + sprung
    ' Whether what stands at a target was made from this unit.
    \ source=path target=path state=namespace
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some root) (sovereign_care .x target state).fil .false
    ?> (./some held) root.get(grove_templates/source_slot) .false
    ?> origin=safe held .false
    | equal[path] origin.path source
  + target
    ' Where the composition a record asks for sits, or none.
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
      base=path [state.self]
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['make]) none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse record.txt_at(['rel])) none
    ? (eq 0 rel.len) none
    | ./some base.weld(rel)
  + highest
    ' The highest invitation number any place of this world holds, in a
    ' scope it keeps or a composition whose places have been numbered.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ nat
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold 0
      \ top [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) top
      = settled (gt record.nat_at(['numbered] 0) 0)
        root=maybe[path]
          ?> (./some kept) (scope_foot/rooted record) (? settled (scope_foot/target record state) .none)
          | ./some kept
      ?> (./some where) root top
      | (sovereign_peek where state).tap.fold top
        \ most [place seat]
        | nmax most seat.nat_at(['invite] 0)
  + pending
    ' The first record, in order, whose composition is planted and whose
    ' places are not numbered yet: one is numbered at a time, so no two
    ' are given the same numbers.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ? (gt record.nat_at(['numbered] 0) 0) acc
      ?> (./some where) (scope_foot/target record state) acc
      ? !(net/live where state) acc
      | ./some (scope_foot/home state.self).weld(rel)
  + numbered
    ' The places a template seeded, given numbers no other place of this
    ' world holds. An invitation's number is the world's: its secret and
    ' its link go by it. A template numbers its own places from 1, so a
    ' world that keeps a second composition, or the same pack twice, would
    ' give two places one number. Each place keeps the number its template
    ' gave it, raised by the highest already in use; a world's first
    ' composition keeps its numbers as they are. Done once, before the
    ' composition is kept, and for one composition at a time.
    \ at=path target=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      top (scope_foot/highest state)
      done=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke (myth/sing ['numbered] (pails/n 1)))]]
    ?> (./some first) (scope_foot/pending state) none
    ? !(equal[path] first at) none
    ? (eq 0 top) done
    | (sovereign_peek target state).tap.fold done
      \ out [rel seat]
      = n seat.nat_at(['invite] 0)
      ? (eq 0 n) out
      | out.snoc([target.weld(rel) (writ/poke (myth/sing ['invite] (pails/n (add top n))))])
  + made
    ' One record that asks for a composition, one step. Where nothing
    ' stands at the target, the unit's template is mounted there. Then the
    ' unit's table is written beneath it, read off its norms, wherever it
    ' differs from what is there. Then its places are given numbers no
    ' other place of this world holds (scope_foot/numbered). Then the
    ' record takes what makes it a
    ' scope this world keeps and a composition it takes part in: the root,
    ' this world as the maker, and the root again as this world's side.
    ' Where something else stands at the target, nothing is made and the
    ' record says so.
    \ at=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      self state.self
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['make]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse record.txt_at(['rel])) none
    = base=path [self]
      target=path base.weld(rel)
      part=myth
        . (myth/sing ['root] (safe 0 .x target))
          put(['maker] (pails/n (quip_val self)))
          put(['side] (safe 0 .x target))
      kept=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke part)]]
    ? (eq 0 rel.len) none
    ? !(net/live target state) (scope_foot/planted at record link.path target state)
    ? !(scope_foot/sprung link.path target state) (scope_foot/refused at record 'scope_occupied)
    = rows (weave/tabled (weave/unit link.path state) target state)
    ? (gt rows.len 0) rows
    ? (maybe/is_some (scope_foot/rooted record)) none
    ? (eq 0 record.nat_at(['numbered] 0)) (scope_foot/numbered at target state)
    kept
  + invitation
    ' The link to the invitation this world minted under a number, for
    ' whichever scope it keeps holds the place; none when none does.
    \ id=nat state=namespace
    ^ maybe[scope/link]
    = none=maybe[scope/link] .none
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted record) acc
      ?> (./some at) (scope/placed root id state) acc
      | scope/linked root at state
  + answer
    \ outcome=maybe[pail] now=namespace
    ^ [nat str str]
    ?> (./some refusal) outcome [200 "" ""]
    [409 "" ""]
  + plan
    \ now=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    | ./ok (scope_foot/all now)
  + stopped
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some version) binding.fil .true
    | gt (unpin version.myth).nat_at(['stop] 0) 0
  + tend
    ' A foot for one rule: it is told each commit, reads the world as it
    ' then stands, and asks for the writes the rule answers, until the
    ' rule answers none. A pack's own hand is such a rule (what its world
    ' should write, given everything it holds) and nothing else: this is
    ' the loop every one of them runs.
    \ rule={\ namespace}row[[p=path q=writ]] init=feet/task/init self=nat
    ^ nat
    = plan
        \ now=namespace
        ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
        | ./ok (rule now)
    ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state 0))
    % turns=nat 0
    ^ nat
    = ;[message caps] (Recv[scope_foot/task] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    ? message
     > (./committed epoch)
      ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state epoch))
      | _ turns
     > (./state request held)
      ; (? (eq 0 (rule held).len) 0 (Send init.parent (feet/gift/admit 0 plan scope_foot/answer)))
      | _ turns.inc
     > (./fact binding)
      ? (scope_foot/stopped binding) turns
      | _ turns
    | _ turns
  + run
    \ init=feet/task/init self=nat
    ^ nat
    ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state 0))
    % turns=nat 0
    ^ nat
    = ;[message caps] (Recv[scope_foot/task] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    ? message
     > (./committed epoch)
      ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state epoch))
      | _ turns
     > (./state request held)
      ; (? (eq 0 (scope_foot/all held).len) 0 (Send init.parent (feet/gift/admit 0 scope_foot/plan scope_foot/answer)))
      | _ turns.inc
     > (./fact binding)
      ? (scope_foot/stopped binding) turns
      | _ turns
    | _ turns
